//# #2890: applying a lambda that carries `[U]` where it is written.
//
// A generic lambda checks to a `CtForAll` scheme, not a `CtFn`. The general
// expression-callee path in the `ECall` arm matched only `CtFn` / `CtStruct`,
// so this call fell to the `CtUnknown` arm and was NOT CHECKED AT ALL --
// arity, argument types and the declared return alike. Measured, this program
// compiled clean and printed 233: the allocation address plus one, with the
// field value never participating.
//
// The controls that make this the narrow case it is: the same lambda WITHOUT
// `[U]`, and the same generic lambda bound to a name before being called, were
// both already checked.

struct Qt {
  w: Int
}

fn main() -> Unit allows Console {
  let v: Int = ([U](u: U) -> U { u })(Qt::{ w: 5 })
  println(__to_string(v + 1))
}
